Content follows the common Puranic telling: Hiranyagarbha; four faces and the four Vedas (face-to-Veda pairing as usually given);
the water pot, rosary, Vedas and lotus; the hamsa (shared with Saraswati); a day of Brahma = 4.32 billion years, a life of
100 such years = 311.04 trillion years; the Brahma temple and lake at Pushkar, Rajasthan (painted from imagination, not a survey);
Brahma muhurta, the period before dawn.
Everything else (score, foley, paper, all painting) is original and generated in code for this film.
Rendering and tools: the Lemo-Opuscar style library (Watercolor Brush style) and its core/ tools.
